<title>HONG KONG: Exceptional boosts National Elec H1 net.</title>
<headline>Exceptional boosts National Elec H1 net.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.99	  vs 3.04</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.30	  vs 1.30</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  109.36 gain vs 28.42 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    74.14	 vs 37.86</p>
<p>    Turnover		     646.91	vs 709.45</p>
<p>    Company name		 National Electronics Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 20-27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 28</p>
<p>NOTE - National Electronics invests in property and makes electronic watches and telecommunications equipment. It proposes a special cash dividend of 1.30 HK cents per share vs nil.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$109.36 million on sales of investment property.</p>
<p>The company said there was a loss of HK$38.03 million during the period under review from discontinued operation of a U.S. subsidiary which was closed in September 1996 and losses from closure of European subsidiary.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
